schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Crypto donations to nonprofits grew 386% year-over-year in 2024
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    More than $1 billion in crypto was donated to nonprofits in 2024, a 386%
    increase from 2023; about 70% of Forbes' Top 100 US charities now accept
    crypto, up from 12% in 2020.
  evidence: 'Cited to The Giving Block (annual crypto-giving report).'
  source_lineage: The Giving Block 2025 Annual Report (as cited in the article)
  interpretation: >-
    Signals rapid mainstreaming of crypto philanthropy among large US
    charities; article extrapolates this trend as relevant to smaller
    nonprofits too.
  uncertainty: >-
    Figures are taken at face value from the article; the underlying Giving
    Block report was not independently checked, and The Giving Block is a
    commercial platform with an incentive to report favorable growth.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/case-studies-nonprofits.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
